34,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I had no idea! It turns out loan transport, crating, and insurance took up nearly a third of the installation budget recently. We really need to be careful about how many outside loans we take.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are concerning. The conservation lab has been down to one filled post since spring, and there is a backlog of roughly two hundred pieces waiting for cleaning and stabilising.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Interestingly, the data shows that weekend head counts climb in rooms with mechanisms or changing displays, but drop where there are only cased objects. People want movement and action.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The structural survey caps the suspended bay at four hundred kilos per square metre, and the evening hire bookings show that open arrangements that cannot be shut up have been damaged by caterers.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,I've discovered that two of our last four openings were delayed because lender paperwork and condition reports arrived after the shipping cut-offs. We must be very mindful of our timelines.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, that backlog sounds stressful! If we pick an exhibition with a lot of items needing stabilization, will the lab even be able to handle it?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Exactly. With only one person in the lab, any exhibition requiring significant conservation work before opening would be a disaster for the staff and the timeline.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, that's a fair point, but we also have to consider the visitor data. If we play it too safe to avoid the lab or the budget, we risk a boring show that no one visits.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"It is not a matter of being ""safe,"" Shion, but of being realistic. If we choose a show with heavy installations or open layouts, we risk structural failure or damage during evening hires.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,It seems we are all discovering that our constraints are quite significant. We must find a balance between Shion's desire for engagement and the practical limits Victoria and Asuka have highlighted.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Victoria"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,I wonder if we can find a show that uses local items? That would save on those huge transport costs I found and maybe even help with the shipping delays Shizue mentioned!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"That would certainly alleviate the pressure on shipping and transport. However, we must also consider if local items still require conservation work, as the lab's backlog remains a critical bottleneck.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, local items are a practical solution, but they must be dynamic. My research into visitor comments shows people return when someone is actually working or talking in the gallery.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we incorporate live demonstrations or working benches, we must ensure they don't obstruct the flow of the gallery or interfere with the evening hire requirements.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is heartening to see us thinking about the human element. A working presence in the gallery could be lovely, provided we don't create more stress for our already tired staff.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm starting to see a pattern! If we find something local, dynamic, and easy to maintain, we can save money and keep the visitors happy. I can't wait to see the candidates!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We must prioritize a proposal that respects our current staffing levels and doesn't add to the conservation backlog, regardless of how exciting the concept may be.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I'll be looking for a candidate that balances that dynamism with the constraints. If we can find a show that is active but doesn't rely on fragile, high-maintenance machinery, we'll have a winner.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will be looking for a proposal that avoids heavy loads in the suspended bay and keeps the gallery floor clear enough for our evening bookings. Practicality must come first.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us hope the candidates offer a solution that is both enchanting for our guests and kind to our staff and building. I am ready to see the proposals.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
