60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Here are the candidates! A: Textiles of the Region, B: Light and Motion, C: Maritime Trade Routes, and D: City Under Excavation. I'm leaning towards A because it's local and would save us so much on transport!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I am concerned about Candidate D. A working conservation bench sounds wonderful for visitors, but with our current lab backlog and staffing crisis, I fear we cannot support it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Candidate B looks promising for the numbers, as kinetic art provides the movement visitors love, but I'm intrigued by D's working bench since people value a human presence.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate B is a risk; overhead rigging in the suspended bay could exceed our weight limits, and open installations are vulnerable to damage during evening hires. Candidate A seems the safest.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Asuka that Candidate A is a gentle choice. It avoids the shipping delays of Candidate C and the maintenance risks of Candidate B, while remaining very welcoming.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, what do you think about Candidate A? It has demonstration sessions with craftspeople, which fits your finding that people love seeing someone working in the gallery!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"That is a very astute observation, Mio. Candidate A provides the human interaction Shion desires without placing an impossible burden on our internal conservation staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"You've convinced me, Mio. If the craftspeople are external practitioners, we get the dynamism and human presence the visitors want without the risk of a boring, static display.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate A also avoids the structural risks of Candidate B and the heavy shipping requirements of Candidate C, making it the most logical choice for the gallery's current state.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It truly seems we have found a wonderful harmony. Candidate A is kind to our budget, our building, and our staff, while still offering the warmth and life our visitors crave.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm so happy we all agree! It feels like Candidate A is the perfect fit for everything we've discovered. Does anyone have any last-minute doubts before we vote?,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I have none. It respects our staffing limits and avoids the conservation crisis, while still being an engaging exhibition. I am fully in support of Candidate A.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,I'm satisfied. It satisfies the data on visitor engagement without the technical risks of Candidate B. I'll cast my vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I have no further objections. It is the only proposal that aligns with the structural and logistical constraints of the main gallery. I vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I feel a great sense of peace knowing we have chosen a path that is sustainable and welcoming. I, too, cast my vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll cast my vote for Candidate A as well! I'm so glad we could find a way to make a great show that's also smart with our money. Candidate A it is!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
